---
import Layout from '../../smarttec-investor/components/Layout.astro';
import Journey from '../../smarttec-investor/components/Journey.astro';
import BrandLockup from '../../components/BrandLockup.astro';
import {pageAccess,privateHeaders} from '../../smarttec-investor/server/auth.mjs';
import campus from '../../smarttec-investor/data/campus.json';
import ArchitecturalCampus from '../../smarttec-architecture/ArchitecturalCampus.astro';
export const prerender=false;
Object.entries(privateHeaders).forEach(([k,v])=>Astro.response.headers.set(k,v));
const access=await pageAccess(Astro.request);
if(access.error) return new Response('Private access is temporarily unavailable.',{status:503,headers:privateHeaders});
if(!access.session) return Astro.redirect('/investors/login',303);
---
<Layout>
<a href="#opportunity" class="inv-skip">Skip to content</a>
<Journey />
<main id="inv-main">
<section id="opportunity" class="inv-hero inv-section"><img class="inv-hero-backdrop" src="/api/investor/concept-manufacturing" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high"/><canvas id="inv-atmosphere" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><div class="inv-hero-copy"><p class="inv-eyebrow">MEAD, OKLAHOMA / DEVELOPMENT STAGE</p><h1>Build the first revenue.<br/><em>Earn the next expansion.</em></h1><p class="inv-lead">An owned starting point. A measured first deployment. A campus built around customer demand.</p><div class="inv-actions"><a href="#campus" class="inv-button">Explore the investment case</a><a href="#returns" class="inv-outline">Test the economics</a></div></div><div class="inv-hero-bottom"><span>8460 US 70, Mead, OK 73449<br/><small>PROPOSED CAMPUS / AI CONCEPT IMAGE</small></span><span>PLANNED FIRST PHASE<br/><strong>8 GPUs / 2 servers</strong></span></div></section>
<ArchitecturalCampus />
<section id="site-map" class="inv-section inv-light"><p class="inv-eyebrow">01 / THE CAMPUS</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>One property.<br/>Three development areas.</h2><p>The supplied boundary survey gives the campus its real shape: a long, narrow property extending south from US 70.</p></div><div class="inv-map-shell"><div class="inv-map-tools"><button id="inv-map-plan">3D site plan</button><button id="inv-map-satellite">Satellite</button><button id="inv-map-tilt">Toggle 2D / 3D</button><button id="inv-map-reset">Full campus</button></div><p id="inv-map-status" role="status">Loading interactive concept plan…</p><div id="inv-campus-map" aria-label="Interactive campus concept map"></div><div id="inv-map-layers" class="inv-map-tools"></div><div id="inv-map-features" class="inv-map-tools"></div><p id="inv-map-detail" aria-live="polite">Choose a building or development area for details.</p><details class="inv-details"><summary>Satellite alignment / designer controls</summary><p>Satellite imagery is dated photography. The default address anchor is approximate. Enter longitude, latitude for the northwest, northeast and southwest property corners to preview alignment. Visual alignment is not survey verification. Changes last only in this browser session; download the registration for your designer.</p><form id="inv-map-align"><label>Northwest <input name="northWest" required aria-label="Northwest longitude comma latitude"/></label><label>Northeast <input name="northEast" required aria-label="Northeast longitude comma latitude"/></label><label>Southwest <input name="southWest" required aria-label="Southwest longitude comma latitude"/></label><button type="submit">Preview alignment</button><button id="inv-map-download" type="button">Download registration</button></form></details><p class="inv-note">Concept massing: footprint positions, orientation and heights are illustrative. Written factory dimensions control over the size of the red annotation boxes. No engineering approval is implied.</p><a class="inv-outline inv-dark-outline" href="/api/investor/marked-survey">Download your marked layout</a></div><div class="inv-campus-grid"><div><p class="inv-big">39.21 <span>acres</span></p><p>Across three surveyed tracts. Existing buildings and proposed development have distinct roles.</p><div class="inv-tract-list">{campus.tracts.map(t=><button class="inv-tract" data-tract={t.id}><span>TRACT {t.id} / {t.acres.toFixed(2)} AC</span><strong>{t.status}</strong><small>{t.description}</small></button>)}</div><p class="inv-note">Buildings A, B and C total 7,118 sq ft according to the owner. Your marked structures 1 (east), 2 (middle) and 3 (west) are mapped as Buildings A, B and C, confirmed by the owner on 9 September 2026. The separate house/office is excluded.</p><a class="inv-outline inv-dark-outline" href="/api/investor/survey">Download supplied survey</a><p><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8460%20US%2070%2C%20Mead%2C%20OK%2073449" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open address in maps</a></p></div><div><div class="inv-survey-toolbar"><button data-survey="all">Full site</button><button data-survey="in">Zoom +</button><button data-survey="out">Zoom −</button></div><div class="inv-survey" id="inv-survey"><img id="inv-survey-image" src="/api/investor/survey-image" alt="Supplied BM Surveying boundary plat showing US 70 at the north, three tracts and existing structures"/></div><p class="inv-note">BM Surveying plat dated 28 December 2025. Pan to inspect; use the original document for dimensions. Screen zoom is not a survey scale.</p></div></div><details class="inv-details"><summary>Survey notes and development limits</summary><p>{campus.easements}</p><ul>{campus.limitations.map(n=><li>{n}</li>)}</ul><p>Tract 2: 495-foot depth in its legal description. Tract 3: 1,200-foot depth. New factory footprints and solar layouts are proposed and are not approved by this boundary survey.</p></details></section>
<section id="deployment" class="inv-section"><p class="inv-eyebrow">02 / THE FIRST DEPLOYMENT</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Eight GPUs.<br/>A defined first step.</h2><p>Two supported servers with four RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition GPUs each. Complete-system quotations and measured workloads determine the purchase.</p></div><div class="inv-stat-row"><div><strong>2</strong><span>Planned servers</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>GPUs per server</span></div><div><strong>96 GB</strong><span>Memory per GPU</span></div><div><strong>1</strong><span>Starter rack concept</span></div></div><p class="inv-note">Per-GPU memory is not one unified pool. Exact rack, cooling, power and support requirements depend on the supported OEM configuration.</p><div class="inv-three-col"><article><span>01</span><h3>Validate a paid workload</h3><p>Dedicated inference, rendering and suitable managed compute. Benchmark customer performance and price the support scope.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Prove collected revenue</h3><p>Measure receipts, power, network, support and downtime. Separate operating cash from equipment capital recovery.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Finance the next capacity</h3><p>More RTX, B300, AMD or Cerebras follows a defined contract and its own engineering and funding decision.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="capital" class="inv-section inv-light"><p class="inv-eyebrow">03 / CAPITAL WITH A PURPOSE</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Know what exists.<br/>Price what comes next.</h2><p>Three financial scopes. One disciplined investment discussion.</p></div><div class="inv-three-col"><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">EXISTING PROPERTY</p><h3 class="inv-number">$2m</h3><p>Owner-reported gross value. Title, debt, valuation and the investment entity's property rights require diligence. This is not automatically investor collateral.</p></article><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">FIRST COMPUTE PHASE</p><h3 class="inv-number">~$330k</h3><p>Earlier planning allowance, including $50,000 working capital. Replace allowances with full quotes and verified recurring commitments before a funding ask.</p></article><article><p class="inv-eyebrow">LATER DEVELOPMENT</p><h3>Separate budgets</h3><p>Two planned 30,000 sq ft manufacturing buildings, expanded compute, solar and storage require separate engineering and financing.</p></article></div><details class="inv-details"><summary>Milestones before releasing capital</summary><ol><li>Title/entity review, complete supplier quotes and a defined customer workload.</li><li>Engineering-approved usable capacity, support terms and funded procurement.</li><li>Commissioning tests and measured network/cooling performance.</li><li>Expansion supported by collected receipts and a customer contract.</li></ol><p>These are proposed safeguards for negotiation. Actual investor rights require legal documentation.</p></details></section>
<section id="returns" class="inv-section inv-machine"><p class="inv-eyebrow">04 / RETURNS EXPLORER</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>What has to be true<br/>for this to work?</h2><p>Change the equipment, customer terms and costs. See the capital recovered, cash required and assumptions behind the result.</p></div><p id="inv-app-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading private scenario tools…</p><div id="inv-calculator" hidden><div class="inv-actions"><button id="inv-new" class="inv-outline">Build my scenario</button><button id="inv-example" class="inv-button">Load labeled illustration</button><label class="inv-outline inv-import">Import scenario JSON<input type="file" id="inv-import" accept="application/json,.json"/></label></div><div id="inv-illustration-note" class="inv-warning" hidden><strong>Hypothetical illustration — not a quote or forecast.</strong><p>The example includes unverified network pricing and synthetic equipment costs. Every input remains editable.</p><details><summary>Read every illustration assumption</summary><ul id="inv-provenance"></ul></details></div><form id="inv-scenario-form"><div class="inv-editor-heading"><h3>1. Equipment and customer revenue</h3><button type="button" id="inv-add-row" class="inv-outline">Add equipment</button></div><div id="inv-equipment-rows"></div><h3>2. Site, costs and funding</h3><div id="inv-global-fields" class="inv-fields"></div><details class="inv-details"><summary>Advanced cash timing, financing and exit assumptions</summary><div id="inv-advanced-fields" class="inv-fields"></div><label class="inv-check"><input id="inv-share-enabled" type="checkbox"/> Show a pro-rata investor illustration</label><div id="inv-share-field" hidden></div><h4>Later capital expenditure</h4><div id="inv-capex-events"></div><button type="button" class="inv-outline" id="inv-add-capex">Add capital cost event</button></details><label class="inv-check"><input id="inv-acknowledge" type="checkbox" required/> I understand these are conditional assumptions; hardware prices and usable site capacity require verification.</label><button type="submit" class="inv-button">Calculate this scenario</button></form><p class="inv-note">Pre-tax monthly cash model. Property, manufacturing, solar and storage returns are excluded. All entered equipment is purchased at time zero; contract expiry is explicit. A positive financial result does not establish available capacity.</p><section id="inv-results" hidden aria-label="Calculated scenario results"><div class="inv-editor-heading"><h3>Your conditional result</h3><span id="inv-result-basis"></span></div><div id="inv-result-cards" class="inv-result-cards"></div><div class="inv-chart-wrap"><h4>Cumulative project capital recovered</h4><svg id="inv-cash-chart" viewBox="0 0 800 250" role="img" aria-label="Cumulative monthly project cash flow"></svg><p class="inv-note">Includes the initial contribution, capital calls, distributions and terminal cash. Hovering is not required: the monthly table below provides exact values.</p></div><div class="inv-actions"><button id="inv-export-json" class="inv-outline">Download full scenario</button><button id="inv-export-csv" class="inv-outline">Download monthly ledger</button><button id="inv-print" class="inv-outline">Print investor summary</button><button id="inv-stress" class="inv-outline">Compare a downside case</button><button id="inv-matrix" class="inv-outline">Occupancy × price sensitivity</button><button id="inv-price-floor" class="inv-outline">Find required modeled price</button></div><div id="inv-sensitivity"></div><div id="inv-matrix-results"></div><div id="inv-price-result"></div><div id="inv-print-assumptions" class="inv-print-only"></div><details class="inv-details"><summary>Monthly cash-flow table</summary><div class="inv-table-scroll" id="inv-cash-table"></div></details></section></div></section>
<section id="evidence" class="inv-section inv-light"><p class="inv-eyebrow">05 / THE DILIGENCE VIEW</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Evidence first.<br/>Expansion second.</h2><p>Ownership, demand and operating readiness are the foundation of an investable plan.</p></div><div class="inv-evidence"><div><strong>Boundary survey</strong><span>Supplied document reviewed</span><a href="/api/investor/survey">Download original copy</a></div><div><strong>Property value and legal ownership</strong><span>Owner-reported; diligence pending</span></div><div><strong>Electrical and HVAC capacity</strong><span>Engineering verification pending</span></div><div><strong>Carrier terms and diversity</strong><span>Documentation pending</span></div><div><strong>Equipment quotes and customer contracts</strong><span>Not verified in this package</span></div><div><strong>Issuer and investment rights</strong><span>Terms and offering route to be established</span></div></div><p>Demand shortfalls, uncollected revenue, equipment obsolescence, infrastructure delays and financing obligations can cause a loss. The calculator keeps those tradeoffs visible. No return or liquidity is guaranteed.</p></section>
<section id="questions" class="inv-section"><p class="inv-eyebrow">06 / QUESTIONS, WITH CONTEXT</p><div class="inv-section-heading"><h2>Ask the project records.</h2><p>Answers come from the supplied survey, owner statements and the documented financial method. Missing facts stay visible.</p></div><form id="inv-question-form" class="inv-question-form"><label for="inv-question">Your question</label><div class="inv-login-row"><input id="inv-question" placeholder="Is the property included in investor returns?" minlength="3" maxlength="1000" required/><button class="inv-button" type="submit">Find an answer</button></div></form><p class="inv-note">Curated knowledge search. This does not connect to private chat history or provide personalized investment advice.</p><div id="inv-answer" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="inv-faq-list"></div></section>
</main><footer class="inv-footer"><BrandLockup /><p>8460 US 70, Mead, OK 73449<br/>Development-stage project • Reviewed September 2026</p><a href="/contact">Request a technical discussion</a><p class="inv-note">Private planning information. Securities terms and the applicable offering route require counsel. A password or SEC filing is not an investment endorsement.</p></footer>
</Layout>
<script>import '../../smarttec-investor/client/app.mjs';</script>
